 # Zipline MVP Partner-Confirmed Contract
@@ -37,6 +37,16 @@ freshness_reviewed: 2026-09-15
 
 Zipline answered the core partner questions for the Wonder 1P Drone Delivery MVP. A fulfillment-capable direct-order Quote requires valid mass and outer dimensions before Delivery Intent creation, while a separate mass-optional RDP discovery Quote is allowed for serviceability and KOETA timing features and is never consumed by Intent. An approved standard package within the confirmed limits is a single-Zip package; `DELIVERY_INTENT_STATUS_IN_PROGRESS` confirms successful loading and custody transfer; the exact planned customer drop-off point is not exposed; Dropbox loading summons the Drone; and `loading_window` is advisory rather than an expiration deadline. Zipline can also provision a separate non-production Partner Site, although the concrete access package is still pending.
 
+> [!warning] Owner edit under review — "outer dimensions" (2026-11-02)
+> On 2026-11-02 the vault owner edited the Short Answer above (git commit `96dc6dc`, "Partner contract: dimensions also required") to say a fulfillment-capable Quote requires valid mass **and outer dimensions**. The edit is preserved as written. It is not yet backed by the sources this page cites:
+>
+> - The Create Quote schema ([[Wonder/Wonder Fulfillment/Projects/1P Drone Delivery/Zipline API Doc/Create Quote|Create Quote]]) has `mass_grams` as its only package field; it has no length, width, or height fields.
+> - [[Wonder/Wonder Fulfillment/Projects/1P Drone Delivery/Questions for Zipline - Single-Delivery Guarantee and Multi-Delivery Handling (2026-07-15)|Questions for Zipline (2026-07-15)]] states that Create Quote "does not accept item dimensions."
+> - [[Wonder/Wonder Fulfillment/Projects/1P Drone Delivery/Zipline Platform Reference/Status Codes|Status Codes]] lists `QUOTE_MASS_REQUIRED` for direct orders and no dimension-required code.
+> - The "Quote mass by lifecycle role" row in the Confirmed Contract table below, and the sibling pages [[zipline-sandbox-quote-mass-gating-contract]] and [[zipline-discovery-vs-fulfillment-quote-mass-contract]], still state mass as the only Quote-level requirement.
+>
+> Reconciling reading: the dimension limits (`338 × 254 × 205 mm`) are a **Wonder-side** eligibility gate applied before Delivery Intent (see "Eligibility Service Impact" and Pack-based fit checks), not a field Zipline requires on the Quote request. If the owner meant that Zipline now requires dimensions at Quote time, that is new partner information; add the dated source to `sources` and update the table row and the sibling pages. Until then, treat the "outer dimensions" clause as a Wonder-side requirement, and cite the table row for the provider contract. `freshness_status` is set to `watch` for this reason.
+
 > [!important] Source precedence
 > These 2026-07-30 partner answers supersede the assumption that a no-mass Quote can be used for direct-order fulfillment. Runtime validation and the confirmed Wonder RDP design refine the boundary: Create Quote accepts an omitted or `null` mass for non-binding discovery, but the resulting Quote must not be used for Delivery Intent. See [[zipline-discovery-vs-fulfillment-quote-mass-contract|Zipline Discovery vs Fulfillment Quote Mass Contract]].
 
